WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.668
Back to our law and justice

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.369
lead right now.

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:02.802
Police in

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.004
Jacksonville, Florida,

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.605
are giving the most recent update

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.706
into their investigation

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.241
detailing the moments

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.776
of the racist shooter

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.077
before he went to the Dollar

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:11.778
General Store

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.380
where he killed three innocent

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.748
African-Americans on Saturday.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:15.515
CNN's Isabel

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.351
Rosales has more now on the deadly attack

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.654
that was fueled by racism

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:25.025
Lieutenant Antonio Bailey hailed a hero

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:25.892
for chasing off

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.193
the gunman who later opened

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.995
fire at a nearby dollar general

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:31.131
in Jacksonville. Florida on Saturday.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.033
That shooter first entered

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.234
a parking lot at Edward

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.402
Waters University.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.436
Florida's first

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.937
historically black college.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.040
He could have gone anywhere

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.441
It's not by happenstance.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.142
It's not just,

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.810
you know, on a whim

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.213
that he chose to come to Florida's first

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.349
historically black college or university

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.750
According to Jacksonville Sheriff

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.684
Tiki Waters.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.919
Police have not reported

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.187
finding any firm evidence

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.288
the suspect intended

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.756
to attack the university.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.690
There were students

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.261
that stopped me and

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:01.628
in that

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.295
parking lot

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:05.065
and advised that there were gunmen.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.599
The shooter drove off

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.535
after being approached by Bailey.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.370
To me, the students that,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:10.637
you know,

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.572
we preach the same saying every day

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.274
you see something, say something.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:17.377
And the students they saw, they say it.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.246
And I was able to approach that view.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.347
I would definitely side.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.350
And that is indeed a tragedy.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.553
The scene of the tragedy

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.320
that followed

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.823
now marked by flowers and crosses,

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.558
a community grieving

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.026
three killed Saturday

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.561
in the racist attack.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.329
He hated blacks and he

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.131
I think he hated just about everyone

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.966
that wasn't white.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.534
He made that very clear.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.136
Now, more information

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:43.903
about the gunman

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.371
identified as 21 year

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.973
old Ryan Perlmutter.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.575
Deputies released this edited

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:49.442
surveillance video

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.677
at the Dollar General Store

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.579
showing him in a tactical vest

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.013
armed with a handgun

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.683
and an air 15 style rifle with swastikas.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.650
Drawn on it.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.452
Then he opened fire.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.587
He understood what he was doing

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:02.222
and he understood why he was on

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.457
the shooter. Had no criminal history.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.492
The sheriff says

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.460
he purchased a handgun in April

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.662
and an AR 15 style rifle in June,

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.964
both legally

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.031
despite as a teenager

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.434
being temporarily involuntarily held

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.368
under Florida's

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.470
Baker Act for mental evaluation

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.372
for up to 72 hours.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.006
I don't know

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.541
legally given

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.076
the way the laws are written right now

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:23.910
in the state of Florida

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.278
that there was anything

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.279
that could have been done

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.281
and therein lies the frustration for me.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.015
The victims

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.617
in Saturday's shooting identified

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.119
a store employee, Arnold Joseph AJ Legere

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.522
Junior and customers Angela Corey

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:36.856
and Gerald Galleon

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:37.590
His killing

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.893
leaves a four year old fatherless.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.760
We're just

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.728
trying to figure out

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:42.862
how to tell his daughter

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.531
that her dad's gone.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.532
It's hurtful

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:46.332
because I thought

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.234
racism was behind us,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.103
but evidently is not

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.070
the attack in Florida.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.772
The latest in a number of shootings

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.007
targeting black people,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.209
including at a supermarket in Buffalo.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.443
New York last year

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.745
and at Mother Emanuel

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.346
AME Church in Charleston,

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.216
South Carolina in 2015 angry

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.420
and sad

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.157
to realize we are in 2023.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.627
And as a black person

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.766
we are still hunted

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:22.268
because that's what that was

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.871
that was someone planning

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.408
and executed

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.776
three people

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.147
and a Jake

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.582
we have new information

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.783
from a press conference

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.017
happening right now

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.752
at the sheriff's office

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.054
deputies revealing

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:41.854
that the shooter

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:45.058
previously worked at a dollar tree.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.926
This is a dollar general

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.294
where the shooting happened.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.764
They've also released three on new videos

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:52.232
here.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:52.999
We're not sure

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.500
of the chronological order

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.134
of these videos,

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.769
but I'll tell you what they indicate.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.372
The shooter going into a Family Dollar,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.940
a totally separate store

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.109
And then we have this video

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.043
at Edward

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.478
Waters University

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.947
on the campus there, that HBCU.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.483
And we can see the shooter

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.985
going behind a vehicle there

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.987
and putting on a tactical vest.

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:14.387
And, of course,

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.722
we know that after that, minutes

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:16.389
after that,

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.558
he showed up at this Dollar General.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.892
The final piece of video

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:20.994
that authorities released

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.161
just this moment

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:22.895
is of police

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.931
entering this dollar general.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.766
And that is when you say

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.802
that the gunman took his own life, Jake,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.838
Isabel Rosales

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.273
in Jacksonville, Florida, for us,

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.507
thank you so much.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.341
Chilling video.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.776
There are Saturday's

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:37.844
racist shootings

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:38.544
in Jacksonville

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:39.846
cast a pall over

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.547
what was supposed to be a day

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.448
celebrating.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.618
60 years of progress on civil rights

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:46.119
in America.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.521
Activists gathered on the National Mall

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.689
in Washington, D.C.,

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:52.592
to commemorate the 60th anniversary

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.894
of the March on Washington

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.329
for Jobs and Freedom.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.097
And the Reverend Martin Luther King's

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.967
I Have a Dream speech during the 1963

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.468
march, which

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.603
actually today

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.371
is the 60th anniversary of it.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.140
But the commemoration was over

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.541
the weekend.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.809
We're joined now by Nikole

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.344
Hannah-Jones, who covers

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:12.278
racial injustice

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.046
and other stories

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.580
and other topics for The New York Times

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.282
Magazine and won a Pulitzer Prize

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:16.883
for the magazine's

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.151
landmark 1619

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.819
project describing the transatlantic

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.888
slave trade and its legacy.

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:23.156
First of all,

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:24.957
Nikole, if

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.694
if it's okay if I call you Nikole

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.763
What's your reaction to this horrible

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.432
shooting happening

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:34.767
on the 60th on the commemoration day

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.636
at least of the 60th

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.405
anniversary of the March on Washington

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.441
for Jobs and Freedom

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.877
Well, I think that it is

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:48.781
an awful and far to common reminder

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:51.517
that as we seek to mark

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.887
racism, racial injustice

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.222
as a thing of the past,

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.191
that it is with us

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:00.293
every day, that we have not banished

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.929
that ugly side of ourselves as Americans.

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:05.431
And many people were saying

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.833
the 60th anniversary

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:09.936
of the March on Washington, as you know,

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:11.471
talking about what

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:13.539
we were fighting against a long time ago.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:14.173
But in fact,

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.942
it was evoking a history

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:16.442
to say

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.344
that the struggle for equality,

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.446
the struggle to end racism

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.850
the struggle to ensure and secure

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:24.951
black Americans rights

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.853
and for citizenship continues.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.488
And this is just

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:31.124
a very devastating example of that.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:34.660
Obviously, some things have improved

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:38.097
for African-Americans, for civil rights

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:38.865
and voting rights

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:39.365
and the like

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.434
since 1963 the Civil Rights Act

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.936
and the Voting Rights Act among them.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:48.074
Do you do you think a lot of the racism

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:52.044
is just more politely shielded

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.179
and hidden.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.815
What's your take on how

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:56.883
how far we have come

00:06:56.883 --> 00:07:00.486
and how far we need to go as a society?

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:00.953
Yes.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:03.022
I mean I absolutely would not pretend

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.223
that America

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:07.960
into 2023 is the same as America in 1963.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.930
But what's also clear is that

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.865
we have forward progress

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.834
and then we see retrenchment

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:16.369
and we are clearly

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.137
in a period of retrenchment.

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:20.373
So you know on most measures

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.176
the Black-White poverty rate,

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:25.278
if you look at unemployment rate

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:25.645
for black

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:26.879
Americans, is still twice

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:27.947
that of white Americans.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.015
The racial wealth gap

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.183
has remained unchanged

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:32.385
for black Americans since Dr.

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.820
King was assassinated.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.822
And the fact that we still see

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:37.356
racialized violence

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.991
regularly in this country

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:41.994
shows that we still do have a long ways

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:42.762
to go.

00:07:42.762 --> 00:07:43.729
Now, the Supreme Court

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:44.397
struck down

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:45.198
affirmative action,

00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:46.532
which was trying to help address

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:47.500
that legacy.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.701
We know that the

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:49.802
Supreme Court

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:50.870
struck down

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.472
the heart of the Voting Rights Act

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:53.406
and that it is harder

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:54.340
for black Americans

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.542
to vote than it was ten years ago.

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.411
So I think that in America,

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.046
we become sometimes obsessed

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:00.813
with this notion

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:02.582
that progress, forward

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:04.217
progress is inevitable,

00:08:04.217 --> 00:08:06.719
but backward progress happens

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:07.820
in this country as well.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.121
And whether we're moving forward

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:09.789
or not,

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:11.224
really is largely dependent

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:13.159
upon who we are as a society.

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:14.727
And we are in a society today

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:16.762
that is deeply polarized

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.498
along racial lines

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:21.701
and where too many politicians understand

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.769
that race is the original wedge issue

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:25.905
and are creating the environment

00:08:25.905 --> 00:08:26.239
to see

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:27.340
just the kind of violence

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.475
that we witnessed in Jacksonville.

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:30.376
But the wedge issues

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.545
are discussed differently today, right?

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.981
I mean in 1963

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:35.481
we were just

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.950
three years away from Lester Maddox

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:41.153
a proud, racist

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.689
segregationist in Georgia, becoming

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:44.891
the governor of Georgia.

00:08:46.025 --> 00:08:47.593
Lester Maddox could not exist today,

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:47.960
but Lester

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:51.330
Maddox would not talk the way he did

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.332
then today were he running. Right.

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:55.067
I mean, it's different.

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.402
What are the wedge issues today

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:59.038
that you hear Yes.

00:08:59.038 --> 00:08:59.739
I mean absolutely.

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:02.642
So since 1968

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.678
it is no longer legal in this country

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:07.680
to explicitly discriminate

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.948
against black Americans.

00:09:08.948 --> 00:09:11.918
So of course we've learned over the last

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:13.719
60 years

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:15.488
that you have to use different language,

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:16.956
that you have to use language

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:19.258
that appears to be race neutral.

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:20.927
But this ends the same dog whistle.

00:09:20.927 --> 00:09:22.695
So we can look at,

00:09:22.695 --> 00:09:23.195
you know, Ron

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:25.831
DeSantis running on this platform

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:28.200
against what he's calling woke ism.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.335
But where those of us

00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:32.638
who study history, who understand

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:33.372
the society

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:33.873
that we live in

00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:34.740
and understand that

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.375
that's often coded as language

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:37.143
against black

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:38.611
Americans, as language

